From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:35:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/20] media: apple: vxd: wire the V4L2 device into probe, make
 remove safe, and complete the boot sequence

Round 1 (device run 1, docs/periph/vdec-device-run-1.md) showed two
failures with static causes:

- No /dev/video* appeared although probe returned 0: the round-1
  restructure shipped apple-vxd-core.c without the apple_vxd_v4l2_init()
  call, so the m2m/media/video devices were compiled in but never
  registered.  Probe now registers them again, with a per-step log line
  naming the node.

- The unbind/bind firmware-boot attempt panicked: remove()
  unconditionally ran the V4L2 teardown on a never-initialized state and
  dereferenced the NULL m2m_dev.  remove() now cancels the watchdog
  first, drops debugfs before touching hardware state, and skips the
  V4L2 teardown unless the V4L2 device was registered; every step
  announces itself with dev_emerg + printk flush (vxd_step) so the last
  line before a panic names it in netconsole or the panic log.

Boot sequence now matches AppleD5500 exactly (LoadFirmwareAndStartCore
order), including the two pipe loops round 1 skipped: the
InitializeCoreConfig prologue (entropy-pipe feature flag, clock
save-and-set to 0x1010113, per-pixel-pipe 0x460=i/0x4020=0x20000 with
the pipe status reads) and the clock save/quiesce/restore dance between
the second known state v1 and known state v2.  The firmware buffer is
now GART-mapped before the MTX boot: round 1 programmed 0x6a00 with the
low 32 bits of its DMA address while every GART slot still held the
dummy page PTE, so the fetch address was unbacked.

New knobs: a debugfs /sys/kernel/debug/apple-vxd/boot write trigger
(runs the R1 recipe in place - no more unbind/bind), an
apple_vxd.va_offset module parameter (hex; shifts both the GART slot
and the 0x6a00 fetch address to test aperture-base candidates without a
rebuild), and a read-only PMGR pwrstate observer (the shared PMGR syscon
pattern) logging the ps_vdec target/actual/history fields at boot.

coreId decode (device run 1): 0x630 = 0x03030811 - the unsupported gate
reads its high u16 (0x0303, > 6, passes) and the pipe counts come from
its low byte (0x11: one entropy, one pixel pipe); coreRev 0x640 =
0x70b00 is only ever printed by AppleD5500.  The test plan expectation
"0x0007xxxx" was wrong; the ADT vxd-version 7 most plausibly matches
coreRev[23:16] = 0x7 (unconfirmed against another SoC).

Validated offline only: LLVM=1 arm64 object builds, full kernel
Image.gz + dtbs link, checkpatch --strict.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
